h the climate of the Arctic.","example":"See freedom smiling thro’ the realms of frost,\nAnd glow on Labradore’s inclement coast,\nTho’ darkness sheds deep night thro’ half the year,\nAnd snow invests the clime,—that clime is dear,\nFor there fair liberty resides, and there\nAt large the native breasts the searching air,\nWhere blows the arctic tempests icy gale,\nAnd famine seizes on the spermy whale,","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Arctic#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:219b500cba050addcb","definition":"Designed for use in very cold conditions.","example":"Arctic gear","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Arctic#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:60b3697f06a4b652a4","definition":"The north celestial pole.","example":"","pos":"name","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Arctic#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a9f18b520e73710aff","definition":"A continental region consisting of the portion of the Earth north of the Arctic Circle, containing the North Pole.","example":"I’ve visited the world from arctic to ecliptic, as a surgeon does a hospital, and find all men sick of some distemper […]","pos":"name","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contri